  {
   "n": 16,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "single | Marks +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Two uniformly and similarly charged circular rings and a field point <em>P </em>are shown in figure. If the&nbsp;field at <em>P </em>is zero, then the ratio of the charge densities on the rings <em>A </em>and <em>B </em>will be</p>\n<p><img src=\"media/2c/2ccda2776ede6689241a.png\"></p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>1 : 1</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>3 : 4</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>4 : 3</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>16 : 9</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>Let the rings <em>A </em>and <em>B </em>respectively have charges &lambda; and &lambda;&prime; (per unit length). As the resultant field&nbsp;at <em>P </em>is to be zero, the magnitude of the field due to each ring should be the same</p>\n<p><img src=\"media/a4/a4b6617446a725031f2b.png\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"media/fd/fd409da917fed1157e64.png\"></p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 17,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "single | Marks +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Two positive charges <em>Q </em>coulomb each are placed at points (0, 0, 0) and (2, 2, 0), while two&nbsp;negative charges <em>Q </em>coulomb each in magnitude are placed at points (0, 2, 0) and (2, 0, 0). The&nbsp;electric field at the point (1, 1, 0) is</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>zero</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p><img src=\"media/08/088ffd1ff649110ef718.png\"></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p><img src=\"media/da/da89885333003c9c09dc.png\"></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p><img src=\"media/06/064c8389e575a96e2920.png\"></p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>The two positive charges Q are diagonally opposite in position and at the same distance from the&nbsp;point (1, 1, 0). Fields produced by them are equal and opposite and so their resultant field is zero.<br>Similarly, the two negative charges at the diagonally opposite corners produce zero field due to&nbsp;mutual cancellation.</p>\n<p><img src=\"media/05/05f012f00812d2d813fd.png\"></p>"
  }
